{"title":"Regulatory Affairs Lawyer Roadmap","role":"Regulatory Affairs Lawyer","summary":"A Regulatory Affairs Lawyer specializing in Science & Technology Law works at the intersection of law, technology, scientific innovation, regulation, compliance, and public policy.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Science & Technology Law (B.Sc LLB)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Regulatory Affairs Lawyer specializing in Science & Technology Law works at the intersection of law, technology, scientific innovation, regulation, compliance, and public policy."},{"type":"p","text":"The role involves advising organizations on whether products, technologies, research activities, data practices, and business models comply with applicable laws and regulatory requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential sectors include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Medical devices"},{"text":"Artificial intelligence"},{"text":"Software and technology"},{"text":"Data and privacy"},{"text":"Telecommunications"},{"text":"FinTech"},{"text":"Digital health"},{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Food technology"},{"text":"Clean technology"},{"text":"Emerging technologies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law","Science/Technology","Regulatory Research","Compliance","Policy","Risk Management"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Regulatory Affairs Lawyer” is not generally a single regulated professional designation. The exact responsibilities depend on the industry and employer. Practising law in India requires meeting the applicable professional requirements for advocates. Sector-specific regulatory roles may also require technical, scientific, compliance, or professional qualifications in additi